    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0599" n="2063" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg2063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.46E9/9–2051: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Ceylon
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-21T20:00:00-04:00">September 21,
                            1951—8 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. Urtels 179, Sep 19 and 181, Sep 20. In event <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mickiewicz</hi> actually sails with rubber, Dept contemplates confidential
                    exchange notes GOC before publicity termination aid. Although Kem and Battle
                    Legislation require rpt to Cong, Dept will endeavor eliminate undue publicity.
                    Guesses or leaks almost inevitable. In any event notes or official US publicity
                    wld not mention sulphur. Dept fully appreciates considerations paras 8 and fol
                    Embtel 181, Emb will receive advance notice any action.</p>
                <p>Re para two urtel 179, Dept believes there shld be no connection possible action
                    under Kem or Battle legis and decision by US participate exhibit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
